91a8fd95-1111-0f21-6b4a-d04d04ea57f4","isOpen":false,"children":["94655e42-4065-e0fd-7ea0-adfe12f2856e","5bdfd7ed-376c-68cd-07c9-5e9f6b2ee4a9","a11b23da-fdec-5684-0d32-f48020573aac","7f852d79-e6b0-1e32-8aa9-2ca0714d4c71","415569ef-c4cd-9758-770f-f7e4b0d2052d","c30bde39-0066-9820-9570-696e8140c3e0","bd5e33cf-dcd6-514b-1e0f-c0840c0da0de","d4de9f13-8f60-51f0-b584-65d2932ebf7e","a0b8664c-62ff-54d4-8181-d828e5bd36ff","7554c31e-b812-5b71-94ba-68da4b6550bb","e4d8ad24-302a-5fbe-8633-9c1bf0c3dfb4","da35f28a-2175-574e-bded-f2cb4717c955","1d20e55b-a4f5-53ad-a1b4-4b0ab5c13cb7","23e490d3-d574-82bf-60c4-e453d69be7fc","fe7bd10d-e50a-7a52-77c6-d5b0f46a8c08","a70f78f4-6df1-161e-b6ed-b734b2be0d52"]},"cef1d9ab-b30a-90db-5007-3accb198971e","17a2d89c-6b84-8833-15fa-75e9f3194101","7efe7236-ccc8-0775-bb4f-56ecaa4a90e6"]},{"uuid":"c31d2255-1aa7-51cb-a871-0c28204a34fd","isOpen":false,"children":[]}]}],"textures":[{"name":"wall_hardwood_broken.png","path":"","folder":"","namespace":"","id":"0","group":"","scope":0,"width":128,"height":128,"uv_width":128,"uv_height":128,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","file_format":"png","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","wrap_mode":"limited","pbr_channel":"color","fps":7,"frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"ad7fe0e5-1c1c-5448-af6e-64eb9dd2df8c","source":"data:image/png;base64,","relative_path":""}],"description":"# wall_hardwood_broken\n\nDamaged state below 40 % HP of `wall_hardwood` (Patch 5): the hardwood piece snapped in half, with splinters (or broken stone) at the break and the upper half (group `hanging_half`) still attached by a thread, hanging down to rest on the ground in front (-Z). Purely visual: the hanging half does not block movement and the wall works the same. The game swaps it in below 40 % HP and back to `wall_hardwood_cracked` when repaired above 40 %.\n\nHardwood wall: a straight segment one column (16 u) long along X, outer face toward -Z. End caps at both ends meet the next segment's cap to form a joint post. Timber (dark squared hardwood timbers with iron bands), 3 m (106 u) with pointed tops and a fighting step behind at 78 u.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y -1..59, z -46..8 units.\n- Texture: 128 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: 27, all in `finished`; the construction and ruined state sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in Patch 5 (the game draws none of them for buildings).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 106 x 16 centred at x 0, z 2\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 78, 6)"}